{
  "id": "Compound::DB00956 - Gene::1576",
  "verbalization": "Hydrocodone, a member of the opioid agonist class, is linked to Cyp3a4 through multiple pathways that converge on the enzyme's regulation. Pathway 1 establishes a direct binding interaction between Loperamide, an opioid agonist included in Hydrocodone's class, and Cyp3a4. Pathway 2 and 3, while less direct, also involve Hydrocodone causing Ureteral Spasm, which is linked to Oxymorphone or Hydromorphone, both of which bind to Cyp3a4. The shared lowest common ancestors—Opioid Agonists and Opioid Receptor Agonists—suggest a broader mechanism of action involving opioid-related pathways. The evidence points to a potential role of Cyp3a4 in metabolizing opioids, with Hydrocodone potentially influencing its activity through the inclusion of opioid agonists in its class. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible dependency on opioid-mediated regulation of Cyp3a4, emphasizing the enzyme's involvement in the metabolic processing of opioid compounds.",
